        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260521-pen%C3%A9lope-cruz-and-glenn-close-star-in-spanish-civil-war-gay-drama-at-cannes",
        "orario": "20:48",
        "timestamp": 1779389297,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Penélope Cruz and Glenn Close star in Spanish civil war gay drama at Cannes Culture Issued on: 21/05/2026 - 20:48 Penélope Cruz leads 'La Bola Negra', the new film from the creators of 'La Mesías', set partly during the Spanish Civil War and following three gay men across generations as they navigate desire, repression and inherited trauma. Glenn Close also stars in the ambitious Spanish-language drama. Meanwhile Lukas Dhont returns to Cannes after 'Close' with 'Coward', a First World War story questioning what courage really means – fighting in battle, or daring to live openly as yourself. Cannes Film Festival: Who will win the Palme d’Or? 21/05/2026 France Rami Malek leads Cannes film on love and the AIDS crisis 20/05/2026 Culture « You have to suffer » : A conversation with Girl in Red and Anders Danielson Lie 20/05/2026 France Pedro Almodóvar chases elusive Palme d’Or as Andy García returns to Cannes 19/05/2026 Culture Carlton Chef: Creating the signature dish for the Jury President 19/05/2026 France Former football star Eric Cantona makes double appearance in Cannes 19/05/2026 Culture 'A naive view of regulation of politics in media' in France, expert says 18/05/2026 Culture Inside Cannes: Five things you don't know about the Festival 18/05/2026 France Sebastian Stan unrecognisable in Cannes drama \"Fjord\" 18/05/2026 Culture"
